# Which operators can reach this Host, in authorized_keys format — one line per
# person. Tracked on purpose: a public key is public, and who may operate a
# board is a reviewed decision rather than whatever happens to sit in one
# laptop's ~/.ssh. Adding somebody is a line; removing them is a line, and
# `bring-up` makes the board's own authorized_keys equal this file.
#
# Nobody needs anybody else's private key. Each operator keeps their own and
# puts its public half here — which is the whole reason this file exists apart
# from host.identity_file.
ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIKTKp2ZMbC8xKgqcun/TKj2lUDUYR7sghfQD4uRJtAL2 eidolon-pi-192.168.1.26
